  "about": "How each people names its own, beyond the names its settled folk are drawn from (folk.json): a tradition, which says what a family is known by and how one of it is called, and more given names, offered to one whose name is chosen (a protagonist) and given to the members of a family a story casts, apart from one another. A family known by a family name (line: family) shares one of its people's family names (folk.json's family), a wife's or a husband's with the rest; a family known by a parent (line: father) calls each by the given name of their own father. The engine knows only these words: line, said, and the slots of said ({given}, {family}, {father}).",
